Z||000000||87MaroonGTKCMO||01-21-2001||11:21 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.bgprod.com/proof.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bgprod.com/proof.html</A> <P>My sister works for this company and she mentioned she was asked to drive their test car around, a Mazda, but she was not sure what it was. She said she was so sick of driving it but they needed to add miles to the car and would tell her to drive it around anywhere on the highway all day.<P>I was looking to buy some fuel system cleaner they make and finally found more information on the car she was driving. It has over 300,000 miles!  I prefer to use Mobil 1 Synthetic because it gives better oil pressure and but don't think it's good to change brands. I was really impressed about their engine teardown results. Apparently they are big sponsors of motorsport racing.<P>Has anyone tried this oil? What harm would it do to change from one brand of synthetic to another synthetic kind of oil? Ohh, and they claim that the oil change interval is 15,000, and that seems too extreme for me.<P>thanks,<BR>sean<BR>kcmo<p>[This message has been edited by 87MaroonGTKCMO (edited 01-21-2001).]||||reg||5
